// Title: Masquerading names
// Severity: High
// Why: Process names that look like core Windows processes (svch0st, scvhost, lsasss, expl0rer ...), names with right-to-left override or other invisible characters, document-like double extensions and "C:\Windows \System32" mock directories used for UAC bypass.
// FalsePositives: Legitimate near-names are allowlisted (dasHost, sihost, taskhost, smsvchost ...); add your own if a vendor binary trips the similarity check.
// MITRE: T1036.005, T1036.002, T1036.007, T1548.002
// Refs: https://redcanary.com/threat-detection-report/techniques/match-legitimate-name-or-location/ ; https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/uac-bypass-attempt-via-windows-directory-masquerading.html
Det_Masquerade()
